  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want \"[Topic Unique] Diablo IV\" shown as \"[TU] Diablo IV\", as the legacy app does, so that long titles stay short in lists and in the reader title.\n\nMilestone: **M4** (validated legacy parity, ROADMAP). Source: operator UI comparison of 2026-11-11, side-by-side simulator captures 07 (pseudos redacted, attached below when available).\n\n### Cause\nLOT-022 left legacy's `filterTU` out of the parser on purpose (D4: \"presentation concern (LOT-010)\", `docs/lots/LOT-022-topic-list-parser.md:15,115`), but no app lot picked it up.\n\n### Legacy @ `87fe0d1c`\n- `Helpers/RangeOfCharacters.m:330-343` (`filterTU`): \"topic unique\" and 8 spellings → \"TU\".\n- Applied to every topic title (`Classes/Topic.m:90-94`) and to the reader title (`Classes/OnlineMessagesTableViewController.m:2437`, `OfflineMessagesTableViewController.m:2349`).\n\n### Scope\n- A pure presentation function in the app (or `HFRModels` if the operator prefers), applied wherever a topic title is shown: lists, Favoris, search, reader title.\n- Reuse the spellings of the test-only copy added by LOT-022 for its differential tests.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Unit tests on the 9 spellings, ported from legacy's list, plus a title with no match left unchanged.\n- [ ] \"[Topic Unique] …\" and \"… topic unique\" render as \"[TU] …\" and \"… TU\" in the list and the reader title.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
  "closed_by": null,
